{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "subsection_title", "parent_tag": "04V1", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\subsection{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{guide-subsection-finite-covers}\n\n\\noindent\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:acc4a732c6067d9897f6e7b4cfdceba56119847520077e4f33648e48cb8ba08c", "source_text": "Existence of finite covers by schemes", "source_text_hash": "sha256:45b2c41666aa39034589da0a7943685484f60094403fb14b213c09bbc989de43", "unit_id": "tag:04V1:title"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04V1", "placeholders": {"CITE_0001": "\\cite[Theorem 6.1]{seshadri_quotients}", "EMPHCLOSE_0001": "}", "EMPHOPEN_0001": "\\emph{", "MATH_0001": "$\\overline{\\mathcal{M}}_g$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\begin{itemize}\n"}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dfa7dd81b1d6f8d14a3afb0aa7bca454a4c20b95d18816e0992a16f6e050a099", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:02b9115b2cd1d5dab8cc414e78326bf9ab2f9eb05d7d77de640b79c36d329af7", "source_text": "The existence of finite covers of Deligne-Mumford stacks by schemes is an important result. In intersection theory on Deligne-Mumford stacks, it is an essential ingredient in defining proper push-forward for non-representable morphisms. There are several results about <MATH_0001> relying on the existence of a finite cover by a <EMPHOPEN_0001>smooth<EMPHCLOSE_0001> scheme which was proven by Looijenga. Perhaps the first result in this direction is <CITE_0001> which treats the equivariant setting.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c9ca1e6c9a6d020c74c2dcba560efda43baca92cca49f00bde3a1dbd14dd7f89", "unit_id": "tag:04V1:p001"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "list_item", "parent_tag": "04V1", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\item Vistoli: \\emph{", "suffix": "} \\cite{vistoli_intersection}\n\\begin{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:309eb9f0802386d34565378467b0709296e68827cf695072c4b7a8473a20acaf", "source_text": "Intersection theory on algebraic stacks and on their moduli spaces", "source_text_hash": "sha256:91103a2cbaad163c91021e09320f1ce39b08497ee956017f47d18adacc4d57d2", "unit_id": "tag:04V1:item001"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "quote", "parent_tag": "04V1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$X \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:27378cbe398ffd0be669b3da0f9978a23108591d50c5dba54feb26f3aaf7bd20", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b74bf4c5c3adbf63a8ba7a38b62c6ba42977eb5bdbad7ff29f5f484c5fd0fe9e", "source_text": "If <MATH_0001> is a Deligne-Mumford stack with a moduli space (ie. a proper morphism which is bijective on geometric points), then there exists a finite morphism <MATH_0002> from a scheme <MATH_0003>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e6e4ea1e1f3ba9ec8066852870d98f6f6d4d3a80a0e27cefeaa691fe8b6c9327", "unit_id": "tag:04V1:item001-quote"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "list_item", "parent_tag": "04V1", "placeholders": {"CITE_0001": "\\cite[Chapter 16]{LM-B}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\item Laumon, Moret-Bailly: ", "suffix": "\n\\begin{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d8b10fa414c52fe947f0d6e3c40e843016c70e78e564a3056a29a9be313f0f27", "source_text": "<CITE_0001>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a94d82eaa4f1f5d6e151f0d6b8ad060ac5d78d5eeb4122815466f7c79eddf662", "unit_id": "tag:04V1:item002"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "quote", "parent_tag": "04V1", "placeholders": {"LATIN_0001": "\\'etale", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$Z \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$Z$", "MATH_0004": "$X'/G$", "MATH_0005": "$G$", "MATH_0006": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2494b57854d15b7234f86ff016e511c63b6e74293c9c8f2c52ba65c674910afc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:63f24188206f6b06d9812534846e258b9f5ff4bd5bb28067f25e7b73d0096f73", "source_text": "As an application of Zariski's main theorem, Theorem 16.6 establishes: if <MATH_0001> is a Deligne-Mumford stack finite type over a Noetherian scheme, then there exists a finite, surjective, generically <LATIN_0001> morphism <MATH_0002> with <MATH_0003> a scheme. It is also shown in Corollary 16.6.2 that any Noetherian normal algebraic space is isomorphic to the algebraic space quotient <MATH_0004> for a finite group <MATH_0005> acting a normal scheme <MATH_0006>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1eb74290e777590c91dff5c66f36124d90f4bed702ee55608fb4d669e3ad3f99", "unit_id": "tag:04V1:item002-quote"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "list_item", "parent_tag": "04V1", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\item Edidin, Hassett, Kresch, Vistoli:\n\\emph{", "suffix": "} \\cite{ehkv}\n\\begin{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9a5d0635a6e41b949fc56aa7aad86e67a21a0617182f9994beeba4e707d373f5", "source_text": "Brauer Groups and Quotient stacks", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b4d055657b2b17ff5ab9fee1b7ccacf96e01da6029ef32377a321e5c2b789642", "unit_id": "tag:04V1:item003"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "quote", "parent_tag": "04V1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{X} \\times_S \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$X \\to F$", "MATH_0005": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:31708a7e74cb201946eb777d8fbfad44bd68bcd1be052775cf63c60b5b30167a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1aa864f3860a1880fb787ecda0bf9f8e49e255a7614c345e6fef8f0d645f99e5", "source_text": "Theorem 2.7 states: if <MATH_0001> is an algebraic stack of finite type over a Noetherian ground scheme <MATH_0002>, then the diagonal <MATH_0003> is quasi-finite if and only if there exists a finite surjective morphism <MATH_0004> from a scheme <MATH_0005>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:316142353595e2e05f9f2b098f0f79d2892c83972f6558618c472522924cdeb1", "unit_id": "tag:04V1:item003-quote"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "list_item", "parent_tag": "04V1", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\item Kresch, Vistoli: \\emph{", "suffix": "} \\cite{kresch-vistoli}\n\\begin{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2bd5f74ba7c695c6023207453504fd961028dfddb5821659a1054105f1d26bb8", "source_text": "On coverings of Deligne-Mumford stacks and surjectivity of the Brauer map", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4f395717825c818b620b0e458b6277281ff0439e43292d6f09e49a6c14b3ef4b", "unit_id": "tag:04V1:item004"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "quote", "parent_tag": "04V1", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:662c08e3656f872f9d814eaee9c23704f06f2fd61af4ce53c319fa53c2a72d66", "source_text": "It is proved here that any smooth, separated Deligne-Mumford stack finite type over a field with quasi-projective coarse moduli space admits a finite, flat cover by a smooth quasi-projective scheme.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5c74a1123ffe01bbf88d971d2af8bef890143f0ea95b60afa041ad09aa4d6c83", "unit_id": "tag:04V1:item004-quote"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "list_item", "parent_tag": "04V1", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\item Olsson: \\emph{", "suffix": "} \\cite{olsson_proper}\n\\begin{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dc5d3bb3549f54f98cfe1c10ec477bca3e790ef6984822ec3bbbcfd61e9f25ac", "source_text": "On proper coverings of Artin stacks", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1a3327c46365b308e27dc799d4f65b9fcd821eb37e6f8714122d195f4cc80cb9", "unit_id": "tag:04V1:item005"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "quote", "parent_tag": "04V1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$X \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$S$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4bd005d27ace169fbf63144e0899468d2c1b8062d59f65525578bcd41736d6bd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f80287995e366d0e394c29affc975671c30f9d07148b8e008a3f22b31a4fa9cf", "source_text": "Proves that if <MATH_0001> is an Artin stack separated and finite type over <MATH_0002>, then there exists a proper surjective morphism <MATH_0003> from a scheme <MATH_0004> quasi-projective over <MATH_0005>. As an application, Olsson proves coherence and constructibility of direct image sheaves under proper morphisms. As an application, he proves Grothendieck's existence theorem for proper Artin stacks.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0f8358f705a5d9c943d283be2767ee12d96e1571fb77f5a38582dcde0ae2b037", "unit_id": "tag:04V1:item005-quote"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "list_item", "parent_tag": "04V1", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\item Rydh: \\emph{", "suffix": "} \\cite{rydh_approx}\n\\begin{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:88bdcdea1c75aacbf39bd15a11849904a9b64a635fd712da84f0e5d085e1944a", "source_text": "Noetherian approximation of algebraic spaces and stacks", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7b11084f7b8ca6ca93a10163c5d1d5ef4ef8855c81f9e7c2734f1ef87c3b3135", "unit_id": "tag:04V1:item006"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "quote", "parent_tag": "04V1", "placeholders": {"LATEX_0001": "resp.\\ ", "LATEX_0002": "resp.\\ ", "LATIN_0001": "\\'etale", "MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$Z$", "MATH_0003": "$Z \\to X$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\subset X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{quote}\n\\end{itemize}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a468d828dcec4004dee51875e5d88140ffe1efa1e393ea34d38522d9aa4ecff4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:50ab38a788209142975318aee94f937556c93cf6866865b7e5ed3d80a5d9eb9d", "source_text": "Theorem B of this paper is as follows. Let <MATH_0001> be a quasi-compact algebraic stack with quasi-finite and separated diagonal (<LATEX_0001>a quasi-compact Deligne-Mumford stack with quasi-compact and separated diagonal). Then there exists a scheme <MATH_0002> and a finite, finitely presented and surjective morphism <MATH_0003> that is flat (<LATEX_0002><LATIN_0001>) over a dense quasi-compact open substack <MATH_0004>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ab888289e89c1d5b17492465ca3260a3aab513c2996c5caa2c8ad39a4e7d4a76", "unit_id": "tag:04V1:item006-quote"}
